meta {
  name: Update
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/USER_UUID
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Updated Name",
    "phone": "+880-1700000000",
    "bio": "Updated bio text",
    "verified": true
  }
}

docs {
  ## Update User — Admin only

  Updates a user's profile fields. All fields are optional — only provided fields are updated.
  If `password` is provided, it is hashed via argon2 before storing.
  Replace `USER_UUID` with the actual user ID.

  ### Request Body (all optional)
  | Field       | Type    | Description                          |
  |-------------|---------|--------------------------------------|
  | name        | string  | Full name                            |
  | email       | string  | Email address                        |
  | username    | string  | Username                             |
  | password    | string  | New password (min 6, hashed before storing) |
  | phone       | string  | Phone number                         |
  | bio         | string  | Biography                            |
  | avatar      | string  | Avatar URL                           |
  | cover       | string  | Cover image URL                      |
  | skills      | array   | Array of skill strings               |
  | website     | string  | Website URL                          |
  | portfolio   | string  | Portfolio URL                        |
  | google      | string  | Google profile link                  |
  | socials     | object  | Social links (github, linkedin, etc) |
  | department  | string  | Department UUID (null to unset)      |
  | student_id  | string  | Student ID                           |
  | verified    | boolean | Email verification status            |
  | role        | string  | `USER` or `ADMIN`                    |

  ### Success Response (200)
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "User updated successfully",
    "data": { ... }
  }
  ```
}
